    {
      "t": "html",
      "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">template &lt;class T&gt; <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_Result_d51722.html\">ara::core::Result</a>&lt; void &gt; GetValue (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_StringView_cfeb8f.html\">ara::core::StringView</a> key, T &amp;value) const noexcept;</pre>",
      "tail": "\n"
    },
    {
      "t": "html",
      "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Returns the value assigned to a key of this KeyValueStorage. This method should only be used to access very large values repeatedly. GetValue may be delayed by an ongoing call from another thread to RemoveAllKeys or Discard PendingChanges, or to SetValue, RemoveKey, RecoverKey, or ResetKey for the same key-value pair. This method uses transaction semantics, it sees the current state of transaction, not the actual physical storage.</p></div>",
      "tail": "\n"
    },
